I smiled to myself as the gentle rolling hills of eastern Wisconsin gradually drifted past my car window. Somewhere, she's out there. She's happy. I just know it. I have to believe that. I hope she believes that I'm happy too. Maybe she's playing with the animals at her parents' farm. I don't know. The car ride back to the airport was relaxing in a way I have never felt before. The weight of 30 ye…

INT. ROOM - DAY

NARRATOR
I walked up to the queue to board, and Nick entered my mind. I was sending him love and hope. I want him to succeed in some small way. I wish him the best, but I know I will never see him again, as long as it's my choice. His voice entered my head again, and I could see his eyes flled with tears. I could hear his voice, flled with pride.

INT. ROOM - DAY

NARRATOR
The attendant scanned my boarding pass. I looked down to see my name, and Nick's voice said, "President Olson." I whispered to myself, "That's me. President Peter Olson."

INT. ROOM - DAY

NARRATOR
This has been Nick and me.
